{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375362-sorcerer-s-crusade-game-need-help","id":1375362,"title":"Sorcerer's Crusade Game - Need Help!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-17T19:10:10-07:00","id":1375362,"title":"Sorcerer's Crusade Game - Need Help!","content":"I am doing A Sorcerer's Crusade Game soon and could use some help. <br /> <br /> I want to revise the setting a fair bit and would like to place the rise of the Council of Nine in 1600. <br /> <br /> In this iteration of Mage, the backdrop is different, but what I need help with is the notion of what is happening in Europe in this world that is relevant to mages. I know the basic history of the renaissance fairly well, but not in super fine detail. <br /> <br /> Anyway, here's the changes. These are relevant to the 1600's and not reflective of any setting elements later in the timeline. The magical styles of the Traditions are largely unchanged, just their histories. some of the traditions are largely unchanged, but some have had a serous shift. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#3a3a3a\"><b>Ahli'Batin</b></span></span></span>: A tradition of mystical miracle workers based in the Arab Peninsula (and the go between from Persia to Africa) who foresaw the rise of Islam in the 7th century and chose to surrender elements of their culture to it, thus being transformed and forced to watch their old way of life and magic die and see their new generation of apprentices be members of a strange new faith; but given incredible power to make their mark on this religion and be at the centre of a powerful new movement. This Alienated their traditional allies, the Taftani and various African magical orders who refused to submit to the patriarchal and hierarchal cultural structure of the new religion of their homelands. <br /> <br /> <b>Kha'vadi/Dreamspeakers: </b>An order of sub Saharan African mages. Originally united due to the threat of Islam and the destruction of their traditional temples, religious orders, cultures and ways of life. A coalition of many smaller groups that cam together to resist the hardships they faced at the hands of extreme religious violence in the 7th and 8th centuries. Pushed out of Saharan Africa and forced into southern lands, where they met with a mix of hostility and openness and sympathy from local magical orders. Never persecuted by the Batini, more so muslim sleepers. The Kha'Vadi is a respected, powerful and populous tradition by the present day (in setting). <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#3a3a3a\"><b>Sahajiya: </b></span></span></span>An order of seers and mystics hailing from Persian and India and traditional frenemies/allies of the Ahli'Batin, Chakravanti and Taftani. Widely respected by many magical fellowships for their insightful seers and accurate predictions. A key part of the gathering of the Council of 9, as many members are motivated by the seers repeated and ominous warnings of mutual destruction of all mystical fellowships seeking Ascension at the hands of the new Order of Reason (MAJOR PLOT ELEMENT HERE). <br /> <br /> <b>Order of Hermes: </b>A powerful and fairly militant order that was once the second most powerful order of Europe. More cohesive than the christian magi that it organized itself to resist, but less widely influential to be sure. The Order of Hermes was never the major player of Europe, but an order that came together to safeguard itself from violent assimilation at the hands of christian magi. Mainly comprised of the last few (non christian) Roman magical orders, The Order of Hermes was not predisposed to cooperation or continued conglomeration except for the fact that they were direly threatened by the existence of extremely violent and intolerant christian magi. Almost a millennium of cooperation has forged Hermes into a singular magical order however. <br /> <br /> <b>Celestial Chorus: </b>An order of christian magi that was pushed onto the fringes by their peers in the Messianic Voices and eventually violently exiled for their resistance to the merger of between the magi of Reason and the Christian establishment. Once nearly wiped out by their fellow christian magi for sheltering Cathars and Gnostics, the Chorus learned to harbour their tolerance of 'fringe' Christians more secretly. Never a powerful group within the christian magical establishment and long treated with disrespect by the magi within it that were more prestigious. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#3a3a3a\"><b>Chakravanti: </b></span></span></span>An order of magi from India, predominantly united from awakened Brahmans seeking to bring harmony and balance to the karmic forces of the Telurian. Very little has changed here, they are the most powerful magical order of India and brought to the council by their traditional allies, the sahajyia, albeit with great resistance from the Akashayana and some others. <br /> <br /> <b>Akashayana: </b>One of the great magical orders of East Asia. Deeply rooted in an interfaith syncretic mystical philosophy. Deeply opposed to the presence of the Chakravanti. mostly the same as in cannon. <br /> <br /> <b>Solificati: </b>Once a member of the powerful Order of Reason, then, a renunciate from that union and a key part of the council of Nine, the Solificati had no great betrayer and instead, have remained a powerful tradition. They now practice a form of mystical artifice increasingly similar to the Artificers and Craftmasons of the order they once joined, though unlike them, they are firmly entrenched in mystical philosophy of Ascension and have little of the intolerance characteristic of the Order of Reason. Criticized for embracing Daedelan tools but too prestigious to put down, the Solficati are a powerful unifying factor within the Traditions. Traditionally based in Greco Egyptian influenced cultures, now branching out across Afro-Eurasia and building global ties to other traditions. <br /> <br /> <b>Verbena: </b>The other great Tradition of Europe, much more powerful than depicted in some setting material. Paganism has flourished in secret for hundreds of years after being officially wiped out in various countries. As such, the Verbena, inclusive of many Valdermen, Old Faith and Spirit Talkers, are a secretive but powerful Tradition once again facing violent extermination at the hands of a (Neo) christian order. Having never had respite since their formation in the mid to late 1st millennium (though this was a gradual process) after facing violent oppression by christian magi, they now simply face a new enemy that threatens to continue the extinction effort against them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#3a3a3a\"><b>Order of Reason: </b></span></span></span>A powerful Order of many houses under one roof. The Order has a strong base from the christian establishment and also from the increasingly influential non theistic guilds which have come to join together. Many of the conventions are not specifically Christian but are comprised of christian magi who were once members of the now defunct Messianic Voices. Its history is being rewritten heavily. the long story short is, the awakened Christian establishment (called the Messianic Voices for the time being) ruled Europe more or less, and outlawed or assimilated every other magical order it could. The Hermetics, Verbena and others were all pushed out, but some, like the Celestial Chorus, Craftmasons and High Guild, chose to exist under it paying lip service to its main stream edicts. As the various guilds that were forced to serve beneath the mainstream elite became more and more influential during the renaissance period, they ceased to be the oppressed and became the oppressor. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bI'm searching for some ideas here that tie into my idea of the awakened christian establishment being the real power of Europe and what the situation looks like around 1600 ad. keeping in mind that the formation of both the order of reason and traditions happens a little later on in the timeline. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T07:03:54-07:00","id":1375419,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> 1565: Siege of Malta <br /> 1588: Spanish Armada<br /> 1590: Roanoke colony disappears <br /> 1592: Five-year long European crop failure begins<br /> 1597: Tycho Brahe is exiled from Denmark <br /> 1600: East India Company is granted a royal charter<br /> 1605: Gunpowder Plot<br /> 1618: Thirty Years War begins","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Any technology distinguishable from magic is insufficiently advanced.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12101-nitromidas","name":"Nitromidas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T16:07:01-07:00","id":1375702,"title":"","content":"My three usual go-tos for @1600AD are Elizabethan England, the city of Prague, and the Spanish Empire. <br /> <br /> Elizabethan England, on the one hand, is a period of extreme intrigue and political upheaval, a lot of it driven by the often violent struggles between the Church of England and the Catholic Church. On the other hand, its a place rife with artistic creativity, including the almost period defining works of Shakespeare and Edmund Spencer, among others. There are a number of conspiracies and plots against the crown (the 1584 Throckmorton plot, the 1586 Babington plot, the Essex rebellion of 1601) that included even into the reign of King James (the 1605 Gunpowder plot in which Guy Fawkes and others tried to murder the entire House of Lords and blow up Westminster being the most infamous). Also the rise of the English navy and the war with Spain during the 1580s, which went hand in hand with the early era of Caribbean piracy and English settlements of the Americas (including the mysterious disappearance of the Roanoke colony). And it is the time of John Dee, Elizabeth's personal advisor, astrology and occultist, as well as alchemist and Hermetic philosopher. Some of her other inner circle included her secretary and spymaster Francis Walsingham, her Mistress of the Robes Dorothy Stafford, and the sea captain Sir Francis Drake. <br /> <br /> Prague became the capital of the Holy Roman Empire under the reign of Rudolph II. He was a major patron of the arts and sciences, as well as a devotee of the occult arts. His court was a collection of some of Europe's top alchemists and astrologers/astronomers (including Tycho Brahe and Johannes Kepler , and he did his own alchemical experiments. He's frequently named as the ruler in retellings of the Gollum of Prague legend, and had a lion and a tiger that roamed the castle (which one could easily cast as familiars). There's also a bit of religious strife going on here. The 15th century Hussite movement still cast a long shadow over Bohemia (especially the Czech people), and the recent influx of Lutheran and Calvinist influence among the urban Germans only aggravated things. This would eventually help kick off the 30 Years War. <br /> <br /> The Spanish Empire involves all these peoples going back and forth from the New World (still trying to find the next huge load of gold after the Aztec and Incan stockpiles have already been looted), and also trying to deal with a seemingly endless revolution against their rule in the Netherlands.Plus the failed attempt to conquer England, and various adventurism in Italy. The Spanish Inquisition is active in this period, but a lot of the popular conception of them isn't really true. They are effectively the secret police and really answer to the Spanish crown, not the Pope or the greater Catholic Church. They have always tended to view charges of witchcraft with a great deal of skepticism (and would frequently work to quash witchcraft panics when they broke out, seeing any sort of mob action as a threat to the authority of the inquisition and the crown). By 1600, a relatively competent king has just been replaced by his generally less competent son and his very corrupt chief minister the Duke of Lerma. <br /> <br /> Also, if you don't have it, I highly recommend the Sorcerers' Crusade sourcebook <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/61476/The-Swashbucklers-Handbook\" target=\"_blank\">The Swashbucklers' Handbook</a>, as it has a lot of stuff about the sort courtly intrigue, swordplay, and Shakespearean archetypes that work really well during this period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}